Subject: SOP Multi-Target Semantic Compiler Data Design

Description: Conceptual and logical data model for the SOP multi-target semantic compiler purpose. It defines stable identities, relations, cardinalities, lifecycle, lineage, and quality rules while deferring physical schemas and storage choices.

@ [data_design_uuid] 68bbe853-eb1b-43c1-910c-344bb23be0e4
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] a90af861-ccb4-433f-964d-eff53d7457ad
@ [exploded_uuid] 5c06d284-2a67-4194-a839-ed7ac5bcd235
@ [refinement_uuid] 74be95ac-9139-45c1-9233-fc994549c57b

& [ConceptualModel] has five planes
  + [source_plane] preserves documents, generations, profiles, roles, regions, and provenance
  + [semantic_plane] owns identities, bindings, types, relations, contracts, instructions, programs, state, effects, judgments, faults, and SemanticIR
  + [projection_plane] owns target profiles, capabilities, artifacts, correspondence, loss, nondeterminism, and PackageFamily
  + [proof_plane] owns obligations, fixtures, diagnostics, observations, evidence, conformance, and signatures
  + [runtime_plane] owns admission requests, granted capabilities, transitions, effect states, traces, results, residuals, and reentry
  = must: prevent a record from changing planes merely because a label or backend representation resembles another plane

& [NaturalIdentitySet] is stable
  + Document has document_uuid
  + SourceGeneration has document_uuid plus content_digest
  + Region has source_generation plus region_uuid and exact span
  + SemanticIdentity has identity_uuid plus namespace and context
  + LanguageProfile has profile_uuid plus immutable version and grammar_digest
  + Module has module_uuid plus immutable version and content_digest
  + SemanticIR has compilation_uuid plus semantic_root_digest
  + TargetProfile has target_uuid plus ABI version and profile_digest
  + TargetArtifact has target_profile plus artifact_digest
  + PackageFamily has package_family_uuid plus semantic_root_digest
  + ProofBundle has proof_uuid plus subject_digest
  + RuntimeRun has run_uuid plus admitted_package_identity
  = must: use generated database row IDs only as physical surrogates, never as semantic identity

& [SourceEntitySet] is normalized
  + Document owns one or more immutable SourceGeneration records
  + SourceGeneration owns one DocumentRoleDeclaration and zero or more RegionDeclaration records
  + mixed SourceGeneration requires explicit RegionDeclaration closure for every non-default region
  + each role declaration binds one LanguageProfile, admission class, lowering disposition, execution disposition, effect disposition, and authority scope
  + supersession relates generations without deleting the superseded generation

& [SemanticEntitySet] is target-neutral
  + CompilationUnit references exactly one primary SourceGeneration and zero or more exact dependency generations
  + CompilationUnit selects one LanguageProfile and one or more TargetProfile records
  + SyntaxTree belongs to one CompilationUnit and retains complete source spans
  + ResolvedBinding joins one reference occurrence to one exact SemanticIdentity under one context and version
  + SemanticType constrains zero or more identities, values, relations, operations, or results
  + RelationSignature owns typed participant roles, direction, arity, cardinality, and inference regime
  + SemanticContract governs one or more operations or entry points
  + SemanticProgram contains an ordered or explicitly graphed set of SemanticInstruction records
  + SemanticIR belongs to one successful semantic compilation and owns a target-neutral node and edge set

& [EffectEntitySet] separates request and outcome
  + EffectSignature declares allowed kind, operation, resource class, authority class, reversibility, compensation, and observation requirement
  + EffectRequest belongs to one program operation and one runtime run
  + AuthorityEvidence supports zero or more granted capabilities but does not itself prove successful commitment
  + EffectTransition moves requested to authorized, denied, committed, failed, compensated, or observed under explicit legal transitions
  + EffectObservation records what was observed after attempted commitment and may remain unknown or partial
  + read and write capabilities are separate records

& [ProjectionEntitySet] preserves correspondence
  + one SemanticIR may produce zero or more TargetArtifact records per selected TargetProfile
  + each TargetArtifact belongs to exactly one PackageFamily
  + CorrespondenceManifest relates every emitted artifact region to one or more SemanticIR nodes and source identities
  + LossRecord belongs to one target projection and one or more affected identities
  + ProviderDependency records external model, version, configuration, tokenizer, seed when available, and residual nondeterminism
  + TargetCapability records supported semantic feature and proof grade
  + unsupported required capability prevents artifact release

& [ProofEntitySet] makes claims inspectable
  + Diagnostic belongs to a compilation or runtime stage and may cite multiple source locations and identities
  + ProofObligation belongs to one claim and names method, required evidence, and discharge status
  + ConformanceCase owns source variants, expected SemanticIR, expected diagnostics, target observations, and negative assertions
  + ProofBundle aggregates obligations and observations without upgrading their strength
  + SatisfactionSignature binds source, exploded, canonical, processed stages, phase lock, registry, scope, and invalidation
  + cryptographic PackageSignature remains a separate trust-plane entity

& [CardinalityRules] are explicit
  + SourceGeneration exactly_one Document
  + Document one_to_many SourceGeneration
  + SourceGeneration exactly_one dominant DocumentRoleDeclaration
  + SourceGeneration zero_to_many RegionDeclaration
  + program RegionDeclaration exactly_one governing SemanticContract per entry point
  + CompilationUnit exactly_one LanguageProfile
  + CompilationUnit one_to_many selected TargetProfile when compilation proceeds
  + CompilationUnit zero_or_one successful canonical SemanticIR
  + SemanticIR zero_to_many TargetArtifact before target selection and one_to_many after successful requested lowering
  + TargetArtifact exactly_one CorrespondenceManifest section set
  + effectful operation one_to_many EffectSignature entries and zero_to_many runtime EffectRequest instances
  + FacultyCycle exactly_seven accounted faculties by activation or eligible omission under its separate canonical contract

& [RelationRules] prevent false inference
  + describes does_not_imply executes
  + parses_as does_not_imply validates_as
  + compiles_to does_not_imply admitted_as
  + proposes does_not_imply accepts
  + accepts_judgment does_not_imply authorizes_effect
  + imports does_not_imply inherits_authority
  + similar_to does_not_imply same_as
  + target_projection_of preserves source relation without reversing authority
  + signed_by_SJS does_not_imply cryptographically_admitted
  + observed_after does_not_imply caused_by without a causal proof edge

& [LifecycleModel] is fail-closed
  + source_preserved -> parsed_candidate -> role_closed -> resolved -> statically_valid -> SemanticIR_formed
  + SemanticIR_formed -> target_checked -> target_lowered -> proof_pending -> packaged_candidate
  + packaged_candidate -> trust_checked -> admitted or rejected
  + admitted -> running -> returned, stopped, budget_exhausted, cancelled, blocked, or faulted
  + EffectRequest -> requested -> authorized or denied
  + authorized -> committed, failed, or cancelled
  + committed -> observed, partially_observed, unobserved, or compensated
  - never: skip role_closed, statically_valid, proof_pending, trust_checked, or effect authorization through status assignment

& [VersionAndMigrationModel] preserves generations
  + source, profile, module, compiler, SemanticIR schema, ABI, target, proof policy, and runtime profile versions are separately identified
  + compatibility is evaluated between exact generations rather than assumed from names
  + migration creates a new generation and records transform, correspondence, loss, new obligations, rollback, and supersession
  + historic signatures and target artifacts remain queryable as historical evidence
  + revocation changes admissibility without erasing prior existence

& [QualityModel] is observable
  + completeness measures required role, contract, type, effect, correspondence, and proof fields
  + consistency measures identity, version, scope, and relation agreement
  + validity measures schema and semantic constraints under named profiles
  + provenance measures exact source and derivation coverage
  + freshness measures dependency and authority currency at use time
  + conformance measures expected observations within declared target guarantees
  + uncertainty measures unresolved, ambiguous, approximate, provider-dependent, and unobserved states without coercion

& [SensitivityAndRetention] is explicit
  + source content, prompts, provider payloads, credentials, user data, traces, and external responses receive separate sensitivity labels
  + digest and semantic locator do not automatically authorize source disclosure
  + retention belongs to source, build, proof, runtime, and provider policies separately
  + deletion or redaction must preserve required proof and provenance through an authorized tombstone or replacement record

& [PhysicalDesignDeferral] is binding
  + relational tables, graph database, vector index, object store, file layout, binary schema, cache, neural tensors, and FPGA memory are candidate physical projections
  + no physical projection may replace conceptual identity, relation, lifecycle, or authority rules
  + physical indexes optimize retrieval but cannot become semantic truth
  + current purpose signature selects no database or implementation technology

& [DataDesignQualityGate] passes at conceptual and logical grade
  + identities are stable and namespace-bound
  + cardinalities and ownership are explicit
  + essential semantics are separated from accidental storage and control
  + lifecycle transitions are legal and fail-closed
  + lineage, version, quality, uncertainty, sensitivity, and retention are represented
  + physical design is intentionally deferred
